3
00:00:05.949 --> 00:00:10.949
(crowd cheering)
(applause)

4
00:00:13.411 --> 00:00:14.244
Thank you.

5
00:00:16.512 --> 00:00:17.763
Oh my God, I'm so excited!

6
00:00:17.763 --> 00:00:18.763
Hi, guys.

7
00:00:20.254 --> 00:00:21.746
I was like, "Is she in person?

8
00:00:21.746 --> 00:00:22.818
Is she in person?"

9
00:00:22.818 --> 00:00:23.651
I'm in person.

10
00:00:23.651 --> 00:00:25.980
"Please tell me it's not a Zoom and it's in person."

11
00:00:25.980 --> 00:00:27.780
Zoom is over.

12
00:00:27.780 --> 00:00:32.780
I mean, feel like one of the last hard hangs I had,

13
00:00:32.840 --> 00:00:35.360
before the world changed, was with you.

14
00:00:35.360 --> 00:00:36.220
Yes.

15
00:00:36.220 --> 00:00:38.370
We hung hard.
We hung hard.

16
00:00:38.370 --> 00:00:40.450
Walking the streets of downtown New York,

17
00:00:40.450 --> 00:00:42.480
having deep conversations.

18
00:00:42.480 --> 00:00:45.502
And yet, we met when we were, I mean,

19
00:00:45.502 --> 00:00:48.140
in the words of Patti Smith, just kids.

20
00:00:48.140 --> 00:00:48.973
Just kids.

21
00:00:48.973 --> 00:00:52.180
We did a film together in, was it 1996?

22
00:00:52.180 --> 00:00:53.013
I think so.

23
00:00:53.013 --> 00:00:56.550
It may have even been '95, but it was '96.

24
00:00:56.550 --> 00:00:59.950
You were just, you were like my, you know, still,

25
00:00:59.950 --> 00:01:02.540
but I was maybe like, 15 or something,

26
00:01:02.540 --> 00:01:04.070
I think you were like 20.

27
00:01:04.070 --> 00:01:06.700
So to me, you were just the coolest girl in the world.

28
00:01:06.700 --> 00:01:08.930
You were just ultimate rebel.

29
00:01:08.930 --> 00:01:10.810
And then we played half sisters.

30
00:01:10.810 --> 00:01:12.730
Yes.
And, I remember

31
00:01:12.730 --> 00:01:14.330
that the first time I met you,

32
00:01:14.330 --> 00:01:15.700
that was the first time this happened.

33
00:01:15.700 --> 00:01:16.620
You hear about a lot.

34
00:01:16.620 --> 00:01:18.280 line:15%
Now people even say it to me.

35
00:01:18.280 --> 00:01:20.740 line:15%
First time, 'cause I seen you on that big screen.

36
00:01:20.740 --> 00:01:23.270 line:15%
In my mind you were like, a hundred feet tall,

37
00:01:23.270 --> 00:01:25.987 line:15%
and then this little person came out and,

38
00:01:25.987 --> 00:01:28.680
you came out and you were all, we like, you hugged me

39
00:01:28.680 --> 00:01:31.670
and we were shooting a scene in a funeral home

40
00:01:31.670 --> 00:01:34.490
where everybody was saying, "Enjoy yourself,

41
00:01:34.490 --> 00:01:35.920
it's later than you think."

42
00:01:35.920 --> 00:01:37.280
And you were like, "Hello!"

43
00:01:37.280 --> 00:01:39.640
And I was like, "Oh my God, she's little like me."

44
00:01:39.640 --> 00:01:40.750
It's so funny.

45
00:01:40.750 --> 00:01:41.583
Yeah, it's true.

46
00:01:41.583 --> 00:01:45.190
I think one of the number one comments I hear from people

47
00:01:45.190 --> 00:01:47.422
is, "Oh, you're so short."

48
00:01:47.422 --> 00:01:49.422
(crowd laughs)
(Natasha laughs)

49
00:01:49.422 --> 00:01:50.780
And I'm like, "I guess I am."

50
00:01:50.780 --> 00:01:53.447
The other one people love is, they're always like,

51
00:01:53.447 --> 00:01:55.647
"Wow, you're much better looking in person."

52
00:01:56.750 --> 00:01:59.100
I get that all all the time.
Is that a compliment?

53
00:01:59.100 --> 00:02:01.290
I don't think it is.

54
00:02:01.290 --> 00:02:02.340
I can't tell.

55
00:02:02.340 --> 00:02:04.000
But I think they mean it as that.

56
00:02:04.000 --> 00:02:04.930
They mean well.

57
00:02:04.930 --> 00:02:06.810
It's a icebreaker.

58
00:02:06.810 --> 00:02:09.130
But it's also a confidence breaker.

59
00:02:09.130 --> 00:02:11.240
It's also like, "You photograph terribly,

60
00:02:11.240 --> 00:02:13.460
congratulations on your chosen profession."

61
00:02:13.460 --> 00:02:15.010
Yeah. (laughs)

62
00:02:15.010 --> 00:02:17.610
And everything, all your choices are wrong.

63
00:02:17.610 --> 00:02:20.410
But, your hair is the best hair on planet Earth.

64
00:02:20.410 --> 00:02:22.753
Come on.
(applause)

65
00:02:23.867 --> 00:02:24.870
I don't know if you can really tell,

66
00:02:24.870 --> 00:02:26.760
but I have a mullet right now.

67
00:02:26.760 --> 00:02:27.980
Oh my God.

68
00:02:27.980 --> 00:02:31.380
I feel like the last time I saw you, I got up in it too.

69
00:02:31.380 --> 00:02:33.330
It's the best hair in the world.

70
00:02:33.330 --> 00:02:34.630
Does it make you happy?

71
00:02:34.630 --> 00:02:35.490
Some days.

72
00:02:35.490 --> 00:02:36.323
You know.

73
00:02:36.323 --> 00:02:38.190
Oh, come on.
I love it.

74
00:02:38.190 --> 00:02:40.783
I have really good hair days.

75
00:02:41.720 --> 00:02:44.270
Marcel Dagenais, who does the hair on Russian Doll,

76
00:02:44.270 --> 00:02:48.247
he really, he was the one that really said to me,

77
00:02:48.247 --> 00:02:49.900
"No, we're not styling.

78
00:02:49.900 --> 00:02:53.110
You're wearing it, we're gonna own the natural texture.

79
00:02:53.110 --> 00:02:57.100
We're gonna, you know, keep it really red, heavy bang."

80
00:02:57.100 --> 00:02:58.800
And I think I was so scared, you know,

81
00:02:58.800 --> 00:03:01.947
of almost being myself, I think.

82
00:03:01.947 --> 00:03:05.370
And it was such a weird process.

83
00:03:05.370 --> 00:03:09.930
The warmth, the positivity and the response of Russian Doll,

84
00:03:09.930 --> 00:03:13.850
the more I leaned into sort of, my natural, true self

85
00:03:13.850 --> 00:03:17.640
and got away from this idea of pulling it straight.

86
00:03:17.640 --> 00:03:20.520
And I don't mean for fun or for fashion, but I mean,

87
00:03:20.520 --> 00:03:24.330
as an, you know, an alternate persona or something,

88
00:03:24.330 --> 00:03:26.640
this idea that I had to be a way that I was not.

89
00:03:26.640 --> 00:03:29.550
And it really, really helped me, I think.

90
00:03:29.550 --> 00:03:32.483
Well, I think when you,
(applause)

91
00:03:33.750 --> 00:03:37.330
also play a character which I heard you wanna do Pesci,

92
00:03:37.330 --> 00:03:38.530
is that true?

93
00:03:38.530 --> 00:03:40.640
Oh yeah, I always love the boys.

94
00:03:40.640 --> 00:03:44.530
I see Pesci in Good Fellas, I'm like, "He stole my part."

95
00:03:44.530 --> 00:03:45.800
You know?

96
00:03:45.800 --> 00:03:48.240
Would you ever play him in a movie?

97
00:03:48.240 --> 00:03:49.730
If it came up, I would.

98
00:03:49.730 --> 00:03:53.300
I think it would be scary to do, but I would do it anyway.

99
00:03:53.300 --> 00:03:55.840
You as Joe Pesci needs to happen.

100
00:03:55.840 --> 00:03:56.713
Okay, I think.

101
00:03:57.860 --> 00:04:00.044
I like that everybody almost applauded and they were,

102
00:04:00.044 --> 00:04:00.986
"We're not sure."

103
